=====================================================================
Edward Tufte's work
=====================================================================

This repository explains Edward Tufte's principles in its own words. Quotations are brief,
attributed to book and page, and used for commentary and instruction. They remain the property of
their copyright holders. The books are published by Graphics Press:

  - The Visual Display of Quantitative Information (2nd ed., 2001)
  - Envisioning Information (1990)
  - Visual Explanations (1997)
  - Beautiful Evidence (2006)
  - The Cognitive Style of PowerPoint (2nd ed., 2006)
  - Seeing with Fresh Eyes (2020)

This project is not affiliated with or endorsed by Edward Tufte or Graphics Press.

=====================================================================
Material derived from jpoindexter/tufte-skills (MIT)
=====================================================================

Source: https://github.com/jpoindexter/tufte-skills, commit 9f4c602 (2026-07-29).

No file and no passage of text was copied verbatim from that repository. The following parts of
this repository were derived from it: we read its 39 skill files, extracted their factual claims,
checked each claim against the books (and primary sources for non-Tufte facts), and kept only
the claims that matched, rewritten in our own words.

  1. skills/tufte/references/canon.md, "Graphical integrity": the selection of measured Lie Factor
     cases (9.4, 9.5, 2.8, 59.4) and the perceived-area exponent (.8 ± .3).
  2. skills/tufte/references/canon.md, "Data-ink and chartjunk": the selection of the range-frame,
     quartile plot, dot-dash-plot and table-graphic (slopegraph) references.
  3. skills/tufte/references/canon.md, "Not Tufte" and "Known slips to avoid when citing": these
     lists record attribution and number errors we found while fact-checking that repository
     (Pugin vs. Venturi, Tukey, Bateson, Vauthier, the Nature/NEJM table, Begley & Ellis).

